  "known_limitations": [
    "The performance profile is a repeatable production Chromium/Canvas2D stress proxy with disclosed launch flags and a 768x600 viewport; it is not a physical integrated-GPU certification.",
    "The current production bundle includes Phaser in a 1.33 MB minified JavaScript chunk, so Vite emits its non-blocking 500 kB chunk-size advisory.",
    "Automated release evidence in this environment covers Chromium. Firefox and WebKit remain documented targets but were not independently certified in this packet.",
    "Replay output is intentionally bounded to the latest 7,200 deterministic fixed-step input frames; it is a debug/export format, not a replay-playback UI.",
    "The clean-room scan is static process evidence, not a legal opinion or an exhaustive comparison against a canonical hash corpus of every historical SkiFree release.",
    "An initial soak invocation exposed a telemetry-timing defect in its exact-zero reset assertion before the measurement loop began. The assertion was replaced with run-number and bounded near-origin recovery checks, independently exercised in a focused production test, and the complete 20-minute soak was restarted from zero and passed.",
    "Post-correction performance initially showed one invalid host ceiling and two long-frame-ratio failures under load 13.49 on 4 CPUs; an orchestrator retry was also invalidated by its host ceiling while the game ran 59.24 FPS / 2.00%, and a later matrix missed p99 by 0.99 ms. After cooldown, the unchanged complete matrix passed at a 59.80 FPS ceiling, 58.83 game FPS, 2.83% long frames, and 25.00 ms p99. No threshold was relaxed; all variance is disclosed."
